# 6. Financial Awareness

An optional but important feature should help users understand how much they spend on impulse orders.

Build a simple spending-awareness section.

Users can manually enter:
- Order amount.
- Date.
- Category.
- Optional application name.
- Whether the purchase was necessary or impulsive.

Display:

- Monthly spending.
- Weekly spending.
- Impulsive spending.
- Frequently purchased categories.
- Estimated spending avoided through planned purchases.
- Monthly spending trends.

Do not automatically collect financial transactions or scrape banking applications.

Never claim that blocking an app has saved a specific amount unless there is reliable user-entered data supporting that calculation.

Use neutral language.

For example:

"Last month, you recorded ₹2,400 in quick-commerce and food-delivery spending."

"Planning your groceries beforehand may help you reduce unnecessary orders."

Do not shame users for spending money.

